<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115759" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιμύθ-ιον</span></b>  (v. infr.), τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίμυθος</span>
			, <i>white lead,</i> used as a pigment, esp. to whiten the
			skin of the face, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				878
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				929
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Amips.
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Dialex.</u>
				2.6
			</span></i>, etc.; even for the hair, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ly.</u>
				217d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντετριμμένην ψιμυθίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					10.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιπεπλασμένη ψιμυθίοις . . ,
				ἀνάπλεῳ ψιμυθίου,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				98
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				1072
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ ψ. κεχρισμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					7.233b
				</span></i>
			; also used in salves, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				17.7.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.15.3
			</span></i>: for its preparation, v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Lap.</u>
				56
			</span></i>. (Written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιμίθιον</span></b> 
			in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				763.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				789.11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).1390.22
			</span></i> (Andania, <span class="entity">i B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1088.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				3.928.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMed.Strassb.</u>
				p.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, and as v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.88
			</span></i>, etc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιμμύθιον</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i> l. c., v. l. in <u>GP.</u>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> cc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιμμίθιον</span></b>  as
				v. l. in <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
			</span></i> l. c.: 
				Aeol.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψημύθιον</span></b> , acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
				<u>in Theod.</u>
				1.201
			</span></i> H., Id. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				2.241
			</span></i> (
				Ion.
			 acc. to <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				103.25
			</span></i>): 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιμυθιόω.</span>
			) [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> ll. cc., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῑ̆-</span>
			indeterminate in these passages; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῑμῡθίου</span> in a hexam. (<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				75
			</span></i>) might be due to metrical lengthening of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῐ-</span>: cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψίμυθος.</span>]</div>
